--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 146b4dedcb9af3b4ab5fe5794271c3d8, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ticket_Coc1_Cpu_Unseated
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TicketData
  ticketId: ticket_coc1_cpu_unseated
  targetModule: 0
  sceneName: COC1-Copy
  title: Nothing happens after internal cleaning
  description: The unit was opened for cleaning. Since then it does almost nothing
    - the fans twitch and it stops. No picture at all.
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  briefingDialog: {fileID: 0}
  requiredTaskId: ticket_coc1_cpu_unseated
  requiresDiagnosis: 1
  symptomText: Fans spin briefly then settle. No POST, no beep code, no display output
    from any port.
  diagnosisOptions:
  - label: Processor not correctly seated after cleaning
    isCorrect: 1
    feedback: Correct. With no working processor the board cannot run POST at all
      - which is why there is no beep code, not even an error one.
  - label: Memory not seated
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: A memory fault produces a POST beep code, because the processor is
      running well enough to report it. Here there is no beep at all.
  - label: Failed power supply
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: The fans move, so power is reaching the board.
  - label: Graphics card not seated
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: A missing graphics card still allows POST and a beep code. Complete
      silence points further back.
